```rust
/// The system-prompt share of the compaction budget, measured from the prompt
/// that is actually composed rather than assumed.
///
/// `estimate_tokens` is yoagent's own estimator — never a second tokenizer
/// (two copies agree the day they are written and diverge forever after).
///
/// Degenerate case, stated rather than left to an unsigned subtraction: a
/// composed prompt larger than the whole context budget leaves *no* room for
/// messages, which is the honest state — the prompt genuinely does not fit.
/// We clamp the reported figure to `max_context_tokens` so the message budget
/// yoagent computes (`max_context_tokens - system_prompt_tokens`, itself a
/// `saturating_sub`) is exactly zero rather than a wrapped or panic-ing
/// number. `exhausted` says so, so a caller can report it instead of
/// pretending the budget is fine.
pub(crate) fn system_prompt_tokens(composed: &str, max_context_tokens: usize) -> (usize, bool) {
    let measured = estimate_tokens(composed);
    let exhausted = measured >= max_context_tokens;
    (measured.min(max_context_tokens), exhausted)
}
```

