```rust
/// The number of tokens the *composed* system prompt actually occupies.
///
/// This is the value handed to yoagent's `ContextConfig.system_prompt_tokens`,
/// which it subtracts from `max_context_tokens` to get the message budget the
/// compactor works against. It used to be the constant `4_000` — a promise
/// about a string nobody measured (#926). On a project with a large
/// instruction file that promise is false by an order of magnitude, so the
/// compactor believed it had room it did not have and fired on turn one,
/// deleting the user's task.
///
/// The measurement is yoagent's own `estimate_tokens` — never a second
/// tokenizer, because two copies of a rule agree the day they are written and
/// diverge forever after.
///
/// **Degenerate case, defined rather than left to an unsigned subtraction:**
/// a composed prompt at or above the whole context budget leaves *no* room for
/// messages. That is the honest state — the prompt genuinely does not fit —
/// and it is clamped here so the message budget yoagent computes (itself a
/// `saturating_sub`) is exactly zero rather than a wrapped number. The second
/// return value says the budget was exhausted, so the caller can say so out
/// loud instead of silently pretending the session has room.
pub(crate) fn system_prompt_tokens(composed: &str, max_context_tokens: usize) -> (usize, bool) {
    let measured = estimate_tokens(composed);
    if measured >= max_context_tokens {
        (max_context_tokens, true)
    } else {
        (measured, false)
    }
}

/// One stderr line for the degenerate case above, or `None` when the prompt
/// fits — which is every ordinary project, and keeps the common path
/// byte-identical.
///
/// Deliberately **not** gated on `is_quiet()`: `--quiet`'s documented scope is
/// *informational* stderr output, and this is a warning that the session has no
/// message budget at all. Same reasoning as the cost warning, which is also not
/// silenced. Glyph-free under `is_plain_output()`.
pub(crate) fn system_prompt_exhausted_note(
    measured: usize,
    max_context_tokens: usize,
    plain: bool,
) -> Option<String> {
    if measured < max_context_tokens {
        return None;
    }
    let marker = if plain { "warning: " } else { "⚠ " };
    let dash = if plain { "-" } else { "—" };
    Some(format!(
        "{marker}the system prompt measures ~{measured} tokens against a {max_context_tokens}-token \
         context budget {dash} it does not fit, so there is no room for messages.\n  \
         The compaction budget is now zero (stated, not an underflow).\n  \
         Shorten the project instruction file(s) or raise `context_window`."
    ))
}
```

